    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n18124" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Fīdentĭa</span></b> ,
			ae, f., <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>a small town in</i> Gallia Cisalpina, <i>between Parma and Placentia</i>, now <i>Borgo S. Donnino</i>, <i><span class="en">Vell. 2,
			28</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Liv. Epit. 88</span></i>. <i>Its
				inhabitants</i> are called <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Fīdentīni</span></b> , <i><span class="en">Plin. 3, 15,
				20, § 116</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Mart. 1,
			54</span></i>.</div>
